WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:08.171
A live race's result now belongs to the service: places, times and output nobody's

00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:09.766
browser can change.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.674
The race ends when every rider has finished or dropped out, or two minutes after the

00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:15.958
first one finished.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.798
The service records each place, time and output from the progress it saw, and a

00:00:27.798 --> 00:00:30.238
submitted ride takes them from there.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.275
Finish before the result is in, and Results says it is recording; the app asks again

00:00:41.275 --> 00:00:42.738
every five seconds.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.392
Once the service has it, the XP arrives, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.643
What the tests prove: the service's place wins, the race ends on time, and the app

00:01:06.643 --> 00:01:07.688
waits for it.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
